<!-- Frequently Asked Questions -->
<section class="py-5 bg-white border-top">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="text-center max-w-700 mx-auto mb-5">
            <span class="badge bg-primary bg-opacity-10 text-primary fw-bold px-3 py-1 mb-2">FAQ</span>
            <h2 class="h2 fw-bold mb-2">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <p class="text-muted">Answers to common questions about Indian credit cards and our calculations</p>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion max-w-800 mx-auto" id="faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-item border-0 mb-3 cc-surface-card p-0">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq1Heading">
                    <button class="accordion-button fw-bold collapsed bg-transparent text-dark" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq1">
                        How does CardCompass calculate reward values?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faq1Heading" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body text-muted pt-0 small">
                        We calculate rewards using the actual earning rules stored in our database for each specific card. If a card earns 5% cashback on online spends with a ₹1,000 monthly cap, our engine calculates the return up to the cap and drops subsequent spends to base rates. Point redemption values are based on verified redemption options (such as statement credit or flight bookings on bank portals).
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item border-0 mb-3 cc-surface-card p-0">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq2Heading">
                    <button class="accordion-button fw-bold collapsed bg-transparent text-dark" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq2">
                        Are domestic airport lounges really complimentary?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faq2Heading" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body text-muted pt-0 small">
                        In recent revisions (2024-2026), most major Indian banks (including HDFC, ICICI, and Axis) introduced spend-based criteria for domestic airport lounge access (typically requiring ₹35,000 to ₹50,000 retail spend in the preceding calendar quarter). CardCompass explicitly discloses these qualification conditions for every card.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item border-0 mb-3 cc-surface-card p-0">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq3Heading">
                    <button class="accordion-button fw-bold collapsed bg-transparent text-dark" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq3">
                        Can I link any credit card to UPI apps?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faq3Heading" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body text-muted pt-0 small">
                        Under NPCI regulations, only credit cards issued on the <strong>RuPay network</strong> can currently be linked to UPI apps (such as Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm, or BHIM) for merchant QR code scan-and-pay transactions. Visa, Mastercard, and American Express cards cannot be linked to UPI apps directly.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item border-0 mb-3 cc-surface-card p-0">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq4Heading">
                    <button class="accordion-button fw-bold collapsed bg-transparent text-dark" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq4">
                        Does CardCompass guarantee my credit card approval?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faq4Heading" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body text-muted pt-0 small">
                        No. CardCompass is an independent educational and comparison platform. We provide estimates and match scores based on published eligibility criteria. Credit card issuance, credit limits, and final underwriting decisions are made exclusively by the issuing banks.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Call to Action Banner -->
<section class="py-5" style="background: radial-gradient(circle at center, #1e3a8a 0%, #0a192f 100%); color: white;">
    <div class="container text-center py-4">
        <h2 class="h1 fw-bold mb-3 text-white">Ready to find your best credit card?</h2>
        <p class="text-white-50 mb-4 fs-5" style="max-width: 650px; margin: 0 auto;">
            Answer a few quick questions about your spending and get an instant, math-backed recommendation.
        </p>
        <div class="d-flex justify-content-center gap-3">
            <a asp-controller="Recommendation" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-cc-primary px-4 py-2 fs-5">
                Start Recommendation Wizard <i class="bi bi-arrow-right ms-2"></i>
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
